      "id": "seg:paragraph:overview:0010:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:overview:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The following example replaces a read-only [`Text`](text.md) view with an editable [`TextField`](textfield.md), checking for edit mode by testing the wrapped value’s [`isEditing`](editmode/isediting.md) property:",
      "normalizedSource": "The following example replaces a read-only [`Text`](text.md) view with an editable [`TextField`](textfield.md), checking for edit mode by testing the wrapped value’s [`isEditing`](editmode/isediting.md) property:",
      "sourceHash": "fa99acadc47160c6e84f348a3645fb16372e119deebf718d7f272d7416e22730",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "You can also customize your own views to react to edit mode.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\n@Environment(\\.editMode) private var editMode\n@State private var name = \"Maria Ruiz\"\n\nvar body: some View {\n    Form {\n        if editMode?.wrappedValue.isEditing == true {\n            TextField(\"Name\", text: $name)\n        } else {\n            Text(name)\n        }\n    }\n    .animation(nil, value: editMode?.wrappedValue)\n    .toolbar { // Assumes embedding this view in a NavigationView.\n        EditButton()\n    }\n}\n```",
      "documentTitle": "EditMode",
      "framework": "SwiftUI",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
